"- complementary \"Bots and navigation\":\n  - button \"You\": \"?\"\n  - button \"Search bots and messages\"\n  - button \"Create issue\"\n  - button \"Collapse sidebar to avatars\"\n  - separator \"Resize sidebar\"\n  - button \"Fixture Starter Rename Fixture Starter Hi, I'm Orbit. What would you like me to do?\":\n    - img \"Fixture Starter\"\n    - button \"Rename Fixture Starter\": Fixture Starter\n    - text: Hi, I'm Orbit. What would you like me to do?\n  - button \"Switch workspace\"\n  - navigation \"Workspace\":\n    - button \"Inbox\"\n    - button \"Chat\"\n    - button \"Call\"\n    - button \"Draw\"\n  - button \"Projects\" [expanded]\n  - button \"Sort projects\"\n  - button \"New project\"\n  - button \"Agents\" [expanded]\n  - button \"New agent\"\n  - paragraph: No agents yet. Add one from scratch or from a template.\n  - paragraph\n  - navigation \"Tools\":\n    - button \"Routines\"\n    - button \"Triggers\"\n    - button \"Team map\"\n  - button \"Active Threads\"\n  - button \"New or share\"\n  - button \"Apps\"\n  - button \"What's new, unread update, version 0.2.2\": What's new v0.2.2\n- main:\n  - button \"Open Juniper's profile\":\n    - img \"Juniper\"\n  - button \"Rename Juniper\": Juniper\n  - status\n  - button \"Claude Sonnet 5\":\n    - img\n    - text: Claude Sonnet 5\n  - button \"Bot's computer\"\n  - button \"More\"\n  - log \"Conversation with Juniper\":\n    - text: Today 11:27 PM\n    - paragraph: Hi, I'm Juniper. What would you like me to do?\n    - button \"Reply to message\"\n    - button \"Copy message\"\n    - button \"Message actions\"\n    - text: 11:27 PM\n  - status\n  - button \"Attach a file\"\n  - button \"Full access for Verification fixture\"\n  - 'button \"Where this conversation works: Auto\"'\n  - textbox \"Message Juniper\"\n  - button \"Live call with Juniper\"\n  - button \"Call mode\"\n- dialog \"Settings\":\n  - text: Settings\n  - navigation:\n    - text: Settings\n    - textbox \"Search settings\":\n      - /placeholder: Search\n    - group \"You\":\n      - text: You\n      - button \"General\"\n      - button \"Appearance\"\n      - button \"Remote access\"\n    - group \"AI\":\n      - text: AI\n      - button \"Model providers\"\n      - button \"API keys\"\n      - button \"Decision model\"\n    - group \"Computers\":\n      - text: Computers\n      - button \"Local VM\"\n      - button \"Logins\"\n    - group \"Account\":\n      - text: Account\n      - button \"Usage\"\n      - button \"Backups\"\n      - button \"People\"\n      - button \"Activity\"\n      - button \"Experimental\"\n  - text: General\n  - button \"Close settings\"\n  - text: Profile Your details and shared context. Saved as you go.\n  - textbox \"Your name\"\n  - textbox \"Email\":\n    - /placeholder: you@example.com\n  - text: About me\n  - group\n  - textbox \"About me\"\n  - status\n  - group \"Language\":\n    - text: Language The app follows your system language unless you pick one here. Only part of the interface is translated so far — untranslated text stays in English.\n    - combobox \"App language\":\n      - option \"System\" [selected]\n      - option \"English\"\n      - option \"Deutsch\"\n      - option \"Español\"\n      - option \"Français\"\n      - option \"हिन्दी\"\n      - option \"日本語\"\n      - option \"Português (Brasil)\"\n      - option \"简体中文\"\n      - option \"繁體中文（台灣）\"\n      - option \"Українська\"\n      - option \"Tiếng Việt\"\n      - option \"Türkçe\"\n  - group \"Effort for new bots\":\n    - text: Effort for new bots How hard every new bot thinks from its first message. A bot can change its own level; model providers without this level keep their default.\n    - combobox \"Effort for new bots\":\n      - option \"Provider default\" [selected]\n      - option \"None\"\n      - option \"Low\"\n      - option \"Medium\"\n      - option \"High\"\n      - option \"X-High\"\n      - option \"Max\"\n  - group \"Usage analytics\":\n    - text: Usage analytics Anonymous product events — app opened, which features get used. Never conversations, prompts, file contents, or bot output. Your email is only attached if you shared it during setup.\n    - switch \"Send usage analytics\"\n  - group \"Defaults for new bots\":\n    - text: Defaults for new bots\n    - button \"Share as preset…\"\n    - button \"Edit\"\n  - text: Group turns Set the usual maximum for a bot turn in a group. A conversation can choose its own. Maximum turn length\n  - spinbutton \"Maximum turn length\": \"5\"\n  - text: minutes\n  - paragraph: Applies to every bot turn in a group, unless that conversation sets its own limit. Direct threads use the inactivity watchdog instead.\n  - text: MCP calls Set one ceiling for how long a bot's MCP tool call may run. Maximum call length\n  - spinbutton \"Maximum call length\": \"10\"\n  - text: minutes\n  - paragraph: Applies to every MCP tool call a bot makes. A call that runs past the ceiling stops with an uncertain-outcome warning.\n  - text: Parallel threads Choose how much each bot can work on at once. Maximum running threads per bot\n  - combobox \"Maximum running threads per bot\":\n    - option \"1\"\n    - option \"2\"\n    - option \"3\" [selected]\n    - option \"4\"\n    - option \"5\"\n    - option \"6\"\n    - option \"7\"\n    - option \"8\"\n    - option \"9\"\n    - option \"10\"\n  - paragraph: Applies to a bot's 1:1 threads. Extra messages queue until a slot opens. A room turn runs one at a time per bot, and direct messages queue behind it. Delegated work waits for a free thread. Threads waiting for approval use a slot. Lowering this limit does not stop running work; model limits and shared-computer protections still apply.\n  - group \"Routines in the conversation\":\n    - text: Routines in the conversation Run a routine in the chat it reports to, as ordinary messages. Off by default — the work stays in a hidden thread, and the chat only gets the status card.\n    - switch \"Run routines in the conversation\"\n  - text: Automatic recovery Use a backup model\n  - switch \"Use a backup model\"\n  - paragraph: If an ACP model provider (such as Qwen or OpenCode) fails before starting, try a backup once. Work that may have already run is not replayed.\n  - paragraph: Applies to direct bot threads, including Chief and delegated work. Channels are not included. Only this thread switches; bot defaults stay unchanged.\n  - text: Backup provider\n  - combobox \"Backup provider\" [disabled]:\n    - option \"Choose a provider\" [selected]\n    - option \"Verification fixture\"\n  - text: Backup model\n  - combobox \"Backup model\" [disabled]:\n    - option \"Choose a model\" [selected]\n  - paragraph: Permissions stay unchanged; some provider switches need confirmation. Using the backup can incur charges from its provider.\n  - button \"Save\" [disabled]\n  - text: Event log cleanup Trim the logs threads accumulate while they run.\n  - checkbox \"Delete event logs of finished threads after\"\n  - text: Delete event logs of finished threads after\n  - spinbutton [disabled]: \"30\"\n  - text: days\n  - paragraph: Off by default. When on, a daily sweep deletes the event-log files of threads that closed or were archived more than this many days ago. It only removes event-log files — never threads or transcripts.\n  - checkbox \"Trim each event log to\"\n  - text: Trim each event log to\n  - spinbutton [disabled]: \"50\"\n  - text: MiB\n  - paragraph: Off by default. When on, each thread's event log is kept at or below this size. Cleanup only removes event-log files — never threads or transcripts.\n  - group \"Welcome tour\":\n    - text: \"Welcome tour The first-run walkthrough: model providers, permissions, phone, and your first bot.\"\n    - button \"Replay app tour\"\n    - button \"Replay welcome tour\"\n  - group \"Diagnostics\":\n    - text: Diagnostics Versions, configuration on/off state and redacted server, desktop and updater log tails. Review the file before sharing it.\n    - button \"Export diagnostics to a text file\": Export Diagnostics…"